# Website OS v2 core

- Classify the experience before designing it. A creative studio site, product-marketing page, operational application, and internal dashboard should not share the same default aesthetic.
- Read `docs/quality-profile.md`, `docs/experience-brief.md`, `docs/asset-inventory.md`, and `docs/tool-preflight.md` when present.
- For design ambition 7 or higher, do not implement the complete site before three rendered visual routes and a hero prototype have been inspected.
- Treat internal instructions, risk controls, evidence notes, and agent guardrails as private implementation context. Never leak them into customer-facing copy.
- Never invent testimonials, client outcomes, integrations, awards, users, metrics, or project status.
- A technically correct page is not complete until a screenshot-first visual judge and a separate technical QA pass both approve it.
- Report placeholders and unavailable proof honestly; do not mark them visually complete.
